# ── MARK LVI — what never belongs in the repository ────────────────────────────
# Everything listed here is created by the app on first run. A fresh clone with
# none of it present boots straight to the setup screen, which is the intended
# first experience — so nothing here needs to be committed, and some of it must
# never be.

# ── Secrets. Committing any of these publishes them. ──────────────────────────
config/api_keys.json
config/api_keys.json.*
config_clean/api_keys.json
config/certs/
config/whatsapp_web/
**/token*.json                # Google OAuth tokens (Gmail / Calendar plugins)
**/client_secret*.json        # Google OAuth client secrets
*credentials*.json
.env
.env.*

# ── Personal data the assistant accumulates about you ─────────────────────────
memory/long_term.json
memory/*.db

# ── Per-machine caches plugins write beside their own data ────────────────────
# These are learned from YOUR screen: which control on YOUR WhatsApp answers a
# call, in YOUR language, in YOUR version of the app. Committing one does not
# leak anything, but it does hand the next person indices that point at the
# wrong buttons — so the cache is rebuilt locally, never shipped.
memory/whatsapp_controls.json
memory/steam_controls.json
memory/*_cache.json
# The screen agent's remembered plans. Same argument, one step further: these
# name controls the way YOUR applications label them, in YOUR language, at YOUR
# versions. They also record what you have asked it to do, which is nobody
# else's business.
memory/screen_recipes.json

# ── Python build noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# ── Virtual environments ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# ── Editors and operating systems ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Runtime output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
downloads/
screenshots/

# Downloaded Piper voices — 60 MB each, fetched on demand by the providers
# panel. Never committed: they are assets, not source, and which ones you have
# depends on which languages you speak.
providers/voices/
providers/__pycache__/

# ── Working copies kept while a release is in progress ───────────────────────
# Snapshots taken before a large edit, so a change can be compared or undone.
# They are the PREVIOUS version of files that are already in the repository —
# publishing them ships two copies of everything and invites somebody to read
# the stale one.
_backup/

# ── Background tasks (core/tasks) — your tasks, their checkpoints and reports ─
memory/tasks/
reports/

# ── Routines (core/routines) — your schedules, reminders and briefing settings ─
memory/routines.json

# ── Cloud agent (core/cloud.py) — created on the SERVER, never committed ──────
# cloud_state holds the link secret and the certificate's private key; the
# workspace holds whatever the agent and your phone put there.
cloud_state/
workspace/

# ── Local data & binaries ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
data/license.key
.gemini/
*.exe
